    ("intro", "This chapter reports what was measured and what the measurements allow us to say. All numbers come from validation clips, validation tracks or test tracks that were not used for training, except where stated. Each result is given together with the size of the sample behind it, because several of the samples are small."),
    ("h2", "5.1 Experimental Setup and Evaluation Protocol"),
    ("p", "Experiments ran on the laptop described in Section 4.7. The separator is validated on 6 s clips drawn from 16 MUSDB18-HQ validation tracks and 36 Saraga validation recordings, and each stem is scored on between 11 and 30 clips. Three further evaluations use longer excerpts: a comparison with the pretrained backend on 12 Saraga validation tracks (20 s windows, full inference path), a leakage study on four MUSDB test tracks (40 s excerpts), and a check of absent-stem requests on four pop songs. Every figure is compared with two references, the raw mixture used as the estimate and the ideal ratio mask. Three terms are used consistently. \"U-Net only\" is the trained query-conditioned network alone. \"Demucs backend\" is the pretrained 6-source model. \"Final system\" is the hybrid pipeline of Section 4.5 with the competitive mask and the loudness step. Checkpoint selection and the detector thresholds used the validation sets, so the validation scores are model-selection scores and not independent test estimates. The leakage and absent-query studies use MUSDB test tracks, and Saraga has no separate test split. The project tests three hypotheses, which follow from the research gaps in Chapter 2."),
