    ("p", "The weak points are as clear as the strong ones. Violin separation is modest at about 1 dB. Ghatam is included as a query class, but the current model does not recover it, and violin and mridangam requests on songs that lack them still return audible output. The Carnatic ground truth contains bleed [11], so even a perfect model would be scored against imperfect stems. The training and validation mixtures are stem sums, so performance on fully real mixes is not measured [18]. Each stem is scored on 11 to 30 clips, and a mean over so few clips hides the spread that [20] asks for. The Western stems depend on a pretrained backend. The guitar and piano outputs sound alike because both include the remaining accompaniment, a design choice that follows from the missing ground truth. They should be read as approximate melodic extractions and not as isolated instrument stems. Finally, the newly trained U-Net has been evaluated mainly on Carnatic stems, and the Western stems of the final system come from the pretrained backend, so the results do not show equal performance of a trained model across both traditions."),
